This constraint can only be satisfied by graphs where vertices can be 2-colored:
- Two vertices love each other iff they have different colors
- Two vertices hate each other iff they have the same color

For each connected component in the graph of "love" relationships, there are 2 valid colorings (flip all colors or not). Components connected by "hate" edges must have consistent coloring.

