    The problem asks us to assign each new road to be either inside or outside
    the circular ring such that no two roads intersect.

    Two roads (chords) intersect if and only if their endpoints alternate around
    the circle. We model this as a graph coloring problem where crossing roads
    must have different colors (inside vs outside).
